==Trivia==
*In the [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|original English Version]], the Enemy Guide was called the '''Enemy Dictionary'''. After registering enough enemies, it would change to the '''Enemy Encyclopedia''', which it is still called in the upper-left corner of the Enemy Guide menu.
*There are many typos and mistranslations that can be found throughout the Enemy Guide, such as [[Zackie Peng]]'s description missing the apostrophe in "that's".
*Due to character limits, most enemies have slightly different descriptions in [[The Battle Cats POP!]].
*In The Battle Cats POP!, [[Chief Peng]] and [[Dark Emperor Santa]] appear as regular enemies and thus have their own descriptions.
*[[Teacher Bun Bun]] has the shortest description in the Enemy Guide.
*In a previous version of [[The Battle Cats]], [[Ururun Wolf (Enemy)|Ururun Wolf]] had the [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Cat Unit]]'s description, due to a bug.
*[[Kroxo]] is the only enemy to have a semicolon in his description.
*The [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]], [[Ghost Doge]], [[Ghost Snache]] and [[Ghost Baa Baa]] are the only enemies in [[Stories of Legend]] without descriptions, and the Doge Base is the only one to not be listed in the Enemy Guide at all.
*[[The Cat God|Each]] [[Cat God|Cat]] [[Final Boss Giga-God|God]] form speaks in first person in his Enemy Guide entry, implying that he wrote the description himself.
*[[Snowball]] will never attack when viewed in the Enemy Guide.
*In Japanese, [[Idi:Re]] and [[Idi:Ne]] have very different descriptions from other enemies, using exclusively kanji and katakana, even for words that would normally be spelled using hiragana.
*Even though [[Value Meal Cat]] is exclusive to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]], there is an empty space for it between [[Gary Gory]] and [[Metal Snache]] in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]]'s Enemy Guide.
*In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], enemies that were added in Version 1.0.6 onwards have their trait listed whereas base game enemies do not.
*[[Surge Attack]]s, Mini-Surge and [[Explosion]] are the only abilities to have the same descriptions for enemies as they do for cats.
*Immune to Explosions' enemy description was added to the game data in [[Version 13.7 Update|Version 13.7]], but was unused until [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]], which added [[Baki Hanma (Enemy)|Baki Hanma]].
*On release, [[Malizabeth]]'s [[Shield]] ability did not display in the Enemy Guide.

===Pre-13.3===
[[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]] overhauled the Enemy Guide by adding most event enemies, type icons and ability icons. There were many oddities and inconsistencies in prior versions, mostly related to enemies' types, which were listed next to their names in parentheses (e.g., "[[Two Can]] was "Two Can ([[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Black]])".
*[[Angel Fanboy]] was the only non-[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy whose trait wasn't included. Until [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]], [[Bun Bun Black]]'s traits were also missing from the English version.
*Bun Bun Black's traits were listed as Floating/Black in the English version, but Black/Floating in other versions.
*[[Maawth]], [[I.M. Phace]], [[Cli-One]] and [[Cosmic Cyclone]] had their traits listed as "Alien, Floating" rather than "Alien/Floating". Maawth, Cli-One, and Cosmic Cyclone's traits were eventually fixed to be separated by slashes, but I.M Phace's traits were still separated by commas up until 13.3.
**[[Ursamajor]]'s entry was mistakenly updated to say "Alien/Floating" when Maawth, Cli-One and Cosmic Cyclone were fixed, even though he isn't a Floating enemy.
*[[Mr. Angel]]'s trait was listed as "Angelic" instead of [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]].
*Cat God and Final Boss Giga-God had their traits listed as "Cool Dude". In actuality, both are only [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]].
**In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Final Boss Giga-God did not have this "trait", only Cat God, who still has it even after 13.3. The Cool Dude "trait's" Japanese name is 本気 (''Honki'', Serious); this is different from the actual Serious trait in [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]], which was named しりあす (''Shiriasu'').
*[[Red EnerG]]'s name was stylized as [Red EnerG]. This may have been a leftover from BCJP's Enemy Guide, which puts all enemies' names inside brackets.
**These brackets were also present in earlier versions of [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]]; it's unknown when they were removed.
*[[Othom]]'s Enemy Guide entry originally didn't mention his Floating trait. This mistake was later repeated with [[Golem Sunfish]].
*The syntax used for [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] and [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemies' types was inconsistent throughout the Enemy Guide and varied from unit to unit.
**[[Baron Seal]], [[Le'Grim]], [[Mega-Mooth]] and [[Super Hyppoh]], [[Big Peng Z]] and [[Archangel Exiel]] were listed as "(Trait) (Colossal)".
**[[J.J. Jackrabbit]] was listed as "(Red / Colossus)".
**All Colossus enemies added in [[Version 11.8 Update|Version 11.8]] and onward were listed as "(Trait) (Colossus)".
**[[Ragin' Gory]], [[Ultima Beast Naala]], [[Wild Doge]], [[Casaurian Ahirujo]], [[Pterowl Hazuku]], [[Crustaceous Scissorex]], [[Suidae Piggicus]] and [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]] were listed as "(Trait / Behemoth)".
**All Behemoth enemies added from [[Version 11.6 Update|Version 11.6]] to [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]] were listed as "(Trait) (Behemoth)".
**[[Lophiiformes Angaburu]] was listed as "([[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]/Floating/Behemoth)", with no spaces between the slashes.

